A||||0||84Bill||A Happy New Year Story (bit long but true)||||14||
Z||000000||84Bill||01-01-2002||03:05 AM||||Talk about a strange new year.<BR>Last night Melissa says to me clear out of the blue "I want to go to New Mexico" clear out of the blue. She has never been there as far as I know know no one there and has no reason at all to want to go there except to buy Native American stuff.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> was the exact look I gave her..<P>So on to today.. at 6:00 or so she rolls in from work and is sifting through mail as I was hooking up the (portable)dishwasher and she starts yelling OH MY GOD... OH MY GOD.. Over and over so I look at her  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> and ask WTF now! She says I just got a (Christmas) card from my aunt (thinking to self) "should I jump for joy?" Not knowing She has not seen her since before she was adopted some 24 years ago. When she informed me this was a lost aunt I was pleasantly surprised.<BR>Now here is the kicker. Her newly found aunt lives in of all places..... New Mexico! hehehehe. Now here is the best part of all Melissa has found her mother after 24 years! <P>Apparently 4 years ago when I coaxed Melissa to do some searching for her mom on the internet and adoption boards ect. ect. She put up a few and after a month or two she just kinda let it go. <BR>Last week her aunt was doing a family tree and was looking for her lost nieces and nephews and their kiddies to add to the tree, knowing they were warded to the state she did a search right off the program that took her to an adoption search page. So her aunt typed in her families name and WHAM Melissa's post was number one on the list. Her aunt could not believe it at first thinking it could not possibly be true but it was. All the brothers and sisters matched perfect along with some other information Melissa listed. So her aunt wrote short letter and put it in a Christmas card and sent it to the address Melissa had left. Well that address was the apartment we lived in before we got this house last year! Somehow they forwarded the letter to the new address and we just got it the 31st, New Years Eve  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Her aunt left a number to call so we dialed it up and as Melissa chatted I took the letter that had her mothers last known address on it (her aunt had not seen her in 15 years but this was the only address she had)and dialed 411. Welp there was a person matching the name but it was unlisted  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  dejected I hung up. <BR>After a while when Melis did some catching  and calling her sisters and brother and gabbing, we started chatting and she wanted to look up the number for her mom and I told her I already tried but it was a bust. She asked me "did you try the other last name?" I said no and grabbed the phone and dialed 411 again and gave them the new information, BUST AGAIN! So while I had the operator on I said what number can you give me for this address and I rattled it off... One momemt please.. YES I do have a listing for a Patsy ****** (the same name I tried before that was unlisted) I said YES thats the one. The operator says ok please hold while I connect you to ###-###-####!!!!! I wrote it down and Blam the phone was ringing! WOOOHOOO!! <BR>Unfortunately I only got an answering machine so I left my name number and told her that "I have someone here she may be interested in speaking to" and gave the names of her sons and daughters she has not seen for 24 years, wished her a happy new year and hung up. Less than an hour later I got a call from Patsy. <P>on top of the 2 natural sisters and 1 brother that were adopted along with her into of family of 15 other brothers and sisters!!!!!!<BR>Melissa now has a family of 9! more aunts and uncles, Countless Cousins, 2 brothers and 1 sister and several nieces and nephews<BR> <BR>Today was cool  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>||||reg||14
